# Episode 5: Someone From Work

INT. MEERA'S FLAT, FRONT DOOR - EVENING

Meera opens the door. KARTHIK stands there with two grocery bags and one mango balanced on top, already rolling up his sleeves.

KARTHIK
నీ left hand rest లో ఉంది. నా right hand duty లో ఉంది.

MEERA
(fighting a smile)
Mango ఎందుకు?

KARTHIK
Dessert.

INT. MEERA'S KITCHEN - EVENING

Karthik at the stove. Meera sits on the counter, directing one-handed.

MEERA
ఇంకొంచెం అల్లం. ...అంత కాదు!

He flips a pesarattu. It folds into a mess.

KARTHIK
Abstract pesarattu.

She laughs, for the first time since the hospital.

Her phone on the counter lights up. Karthik's eyes go to it.

ON SCREEN: "Arjun: Dinner Saturday? No pressure."

Karthik turns back to the pan.

KARTHIK (CONT'D)
(even)
నీ ఇష్టం.

Meera's laugh dies.

His right hand grips the pan handle, knuckles white. The pesarattu begins to smoke.

MEERA
మీ అమ్మకి నేను 'someone from work' నా?

Silence. The pesarattu burns. Smoke curls up.

MEERA (CONT'D)
ఆ రోజు నేను నిద్రపోలేదు, Karthik. అంతా విన్నా.

He turns off the stove. He doesn't turn around.

KARTHIK
Late అయింది. Tablets మర్చిపోకు.

He picks up his helmet and goes. The door clicks shut.

INT. MEERA'S FLAT - NIGHT

Meera alone. The burnt pesarattu is still in the pan, the mango untouched.

She opens Arjun's chat and types one-handed: "Saturday. Okay."

Her thumb hovers. She sends it.
